[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should I set up alongside this?[0m

  [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m node:test unit tests (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mNode's built-in test runner plus an npm test script. Zero dependencies, runs ES modules natively, keeps the repo [39m
  [38;5;246mdependency-free.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] ESLint + Prettier
  [38;5;246mStandard JS lint and auto-format. Catches real mistakes, but introduces the repo's first node_modules and config [39m
  [38;5;246mfiles.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end browser tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright or similar driving the real page. Highest fidelity for the binder; heaviest setup for a four-field form — [39m
  [38;5;246mI'd skip it at this size.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — just the code
  [38;5;246mShip the modules with no test or lint infrastructure. Fastest now; the pure core then has nothing verifying it.[39m
